  "privacyHeading": "Privacy by Design",
  "privacyTitle": "Your photos stay yours.",
  "privacyBody": "Your library, its records and its face data are stored in a database on this iPhone, and all processing — grouping, search and face recognition — happens on the device. There is no Photos Vault server and no account, so nothing is ever sent to the developer. Photos only go where you send them: your own bucket for backup, your own iCloud, or your own AI key for analysis. Keys are kept in the Keychain and never included in a backup. If you delete the app, its local data is deleted with it.",
