  "privateAlbumHowTitle": "HOW THIS WORKS",
  "privateAlbumHowBullets": "Every code opens an album. A code that hasn't been used opens an empty one, so nothing on this phone reveals whether anything is hidden.\nHiding removes the photo from Photos. This app then holds the only copy.\nWhat's uploaded to your bucket looks like an ordinary photo: a different picture from your library, with your hidden photo encrypted inside it.\nThe decoy is chosen to be about the same file size as your photo, so it doesn't stand out.\nThe decoy never carries your photo's date, and nothing records which decoy holds which photo.\nYour passphrase and 4-digit code together form the key. Neither is stored anywhere, on this phone or in the bucket.\nNothing about a hidden photo is kept on this phone: no file, no thumbnail, no record. That's why this album needs an internet connection.\nThumbnails are downloaded 64 KB at a time, so browsing the grid uses a fraction of the data the full photos would.\nNothing is ever deleted from your bucket unless you delete it yourself.\nAnyone who reads this app's source code can identify the disguised photos and count them, but still cannot open one.",
